IMO the game should not allow this ascension strategy, not because it's
abusive, but because it goes so totally against what any reasonable person
would expect a servant of a god to do in that situation.

A character begins Nethack under the premise that they are supposed to
bring glory to their god. A worshipper who uses a HoOA to change god at
the last second pretty clearly violates the stated purpose of the
adventure. At best, I can see this tactic being in character for certain
classes like Rogues (and contrariwise, it's flagrantly out of character
for Priests).

Another argument for banning this tactic is that if mere mortal Quest
Leaders can see through the superficial effects of a HoOA, then why a
deity should not be able to see through it is beyond me.

I'm no expert at Nethack, and I usually play the game using pretty much
every in-game abuse available at hand, but I refuse to use a HoOA to
ascend, because it is the one abuse I've encountered that really seems to
violate the spirit of the game (even more than pudding farming). If I ever
desired to ascend a lawful Elf, I would use some other way to convert
alignment.

